WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.467
-Welcome back to the show.
-Thank you.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.467
-It's nice to see you
in person, as well.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.501
-Thanks.
-You look great.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:06.167
-In person, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:08.801
I wanted to ask you,
'cause I know you're into --

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:11.200
very into fantasy football.
-Yeah. Very, very much.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.834
-How are you doing this season?
-I'm winning.

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:14.267
-You are?
-Yeah, I'm in first place.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:15.367
-Oh, wow.
-First place.

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.234
If Cooper Kupp
doesn't go off tonight,

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:19.200
then I'll remain in first place.
-Wow.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.701
-Yeah.
-And you play in this league

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:22.300
with your -- with your old pal,
Paul Rudd.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.801
-With Paul.
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:26.567
-Yeah, who is
the Sexiest Man Alive.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:30.968
Just think it would be a little
intimidating to play against.

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.167
-Yeah.
I mean, you know,

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:34.200
it's a funny year, right?
There was a pandemic.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.400
[ Laughter ]
So...

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.868
-So you're saying that
this is not a real --

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:38.868
-Eh, it's like there can be
an asterisk on it.

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:40.133
[ Laughter ]
I think.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:41.767
Like the steroids era.
You know what I mean?

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:43.901
Like, "Really?"
I mean, I don't know.

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:45.400
Been an off year.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.567
-Really?
You think that --

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:47.801
So, this year, you go,
"Eh, sure. Yeah."

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:49.968
-Menschiest guy, I guess.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:51.934
I would say, but --
-Menschiest.

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:53.767
-Sexiest? You know...
-but I'm glad you're winning.

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:54.934
I love that.
Yeah, you're in the lead.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.501
-Yeah, yeah.
-I haven't seen you since

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:57.767
"Nine Perfect Strangers,"
by the way.

00:00:57.767 --> 00:00:58.934
Congratulations on that.
-Thank you.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.000
-That was amazing work in that.
-Thanks.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.801
-And we were talking backstage,
and I was saying,

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:08.601
'cause I've seen you
on Broadway.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.467
I know you were here when you
were in a Scorsese movie.

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:14.000
What do you get recognized
the most for?

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.300
-"Everybody Loves Raymond."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.267
You know I'm not on
"Everybody Loves Raymond."

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:20.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:21.634
-Yeah, you had nothing to do
with that show.

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:23.000
-No, I had nothing
to do with that show,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.367
but if I could get --
Like, maybe, if this could help

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:27.634
me to have 10 less people
stop me and say,

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:29.133
"We love you on
'Everybody Loves Raymond,'"

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:30.934
that would be great for my life
because I'm not on that show.

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:33.067
-You were never on the show.
-Never been on the show.

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:34.367
I'm a fan.
Don't get me wrong.

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:36.501
-Yeah, but people think
you're Brad Garrett.

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:38.133
-Yeah, they think
I'm Brad Garrett, yeah.

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:40.033
[ Laughter ]
All the time.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.734
-I found a picture
after you told me that,

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:45.601
'cause I was like --
Could you make this face?

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:47.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:49.567
This a --
Oh, not bad.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:50.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:52.701
And you can do the voice?
-Yeah.

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:55.067
-All right, let's hear --
You do the voice, and I'll do --

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:57.234
I'll do -- I can do Ray.
-"Ma.

00:01:57.234 --> 00:02:00.267
Ma, Raymond -- Ma, tell Raymond
to stop making fun of me."

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.567
-"Ma!"
-"Ma, tell Raymond

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:03.901
to stop making fun of me."
-"Ma, Ma! Hey, Mom."

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:05.701
-That's the show, pretty much.
-Yeah, we did it.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:07.067
We nailed it.
We should take it on the road.

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:08.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.000
-No, but it is --
It's interesting.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.934
But it's --
Yeah, I'm always like, you know,

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:14.067
"He's really a lot taller
than I am."

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.968
-He really is.
-He's the nicest guy, but, like,

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.434
I'm just not him.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:19.968
-Sorry, so just to clear it up,
this is not Brad Garrett.

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:21.100
-Yes.
-Okay, there.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.300
Just so everyone knows.
Yeah, no.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.601
You're Bobby Cannavale.
I want to --

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:26.234
But I want to talk about this,

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:27.667
this "Sing 2"
that you're in right now.

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:29.734
But first, are you working
on something now

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:31.334
where you're
a Neil Diamond impersonator?

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.834
-I just did a movie in Australia
called "Seriously Red."

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:35.367
It's coming out next year.
And it's --

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:37.267
It's set in the world
of celebrity impersonators.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:39.033
And I play
a Neil Diamond impersonator

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:41.300
who's managing
a Dolly Parton impersonator,

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.434
and it's a pretty fun movie.
-I'm obsessed with this.

00:02:43.434 --> 00:02:44.901
This is --
It sounds fantastic.

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:47.167
-And it's perfect for me because
I'm obsessed with Neil Diamond.

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.000
I mean, I love Neil Diamond,
and, like, I could sing him

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.100
'cause it's
a pretty low voice, and --

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.601
-Yeah.
-And so, I got to sing

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:54.434
a few songs in it,
and it's really -- really fun.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:56.734
-What's your key to doing
a Neil Diamond impression?

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:58.567
-Well, you just got to sing it
with feeling, right?

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:00.367
Because the songs almost
don't make any sense, so...

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:01.801
[ Laughter ]
You know, just --

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:03.434
you just got to
just really feel it.

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:05.701
Like, what the hell
is "Holly Holy"?

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:06.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:08.767
"Heartlight"
is all about "E.T.,"

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:09.834
but, you know...
-Yes.

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.334
-...it makes you
want to make sweet love,

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:13.300
even though it's about an alien,
you know?

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.434
[ Laughter ]
That doesn't exist.

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:16.567
-That was from "E.T.," yeah.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:18.467
-So turn on --
-Yeah, it's like, uh...

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:21.534
♪ Turn on your heartlight ♪
-Wow.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.667
♪ Let it shine
wherever you go ♪

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:26.234
-Wow!
That is a good Neil Diamond.

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:28.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, and, uh --

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:31.067
-It is about "E.T."
-Just about selling the song.

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:32.734
Nobody sells a song
quite like Neil, you know?

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:33.868
-Neil Diamond.
No, no, no.

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:34.868
-It doesn't matter
what it's about.

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:36.267
-You have a great voice, though.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:38.767
I was not surprised to hear this
that you were a DJ at one point.

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:39.934
-I was.
On the radio, yeah.

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:41.334
-In college?
When was it?

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:44.467
-No, I was -- I was about 18,
19 years old, and I was --

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:46.868
I just got a job
on a radio station

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:51.334
that was a motivational
radio station, called WNN.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:52.701
It was --
I guess there was, like,

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:56.100
a minute there where that was --
that was a thing.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.901
And it was -- it was
just motivational speakers,

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:01.267
and it was called
"For Winners Only --

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:04.234
The Winners News Network."
-Wow! WNN.

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:06.601
-Yeah, and I was --
I called myself "Bobby Savage."

00:04:06.601 --> 00:04:09.501
I was on from midnight to 6:00.

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:11.000
-Holy moly.
-And -- And I'd be like,

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.234
"Hey, it's Bobby Savage on the
Winners News Network.

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:15.934
Here's Leo Buscaglia on the --

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:17.868
on hugs
and why they're important."

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:19.300
You know, things like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.634
-Dude, I've never heard of that.
-And I would play, like,

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:22.234
motivational speakers and --
-Winners News Network.

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:24.000
-Yeah, yeah.
-That was a big deal.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.834
-It was a big deal
back in the late '80s.

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:28.534
That was, like, my --
Yeah, that was, like,

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.901
my foray into show biz, I guess.

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:32.200
-I can't believe I'm sitting
next to Bobby Savage.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.868
-Yeah, I know.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:38.100
-You know, it was very cute
before the show.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:41.334
We can talk about this, but you
were FaceTiming with your --

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:42.367
your kid.
-My kids, yeah.

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:44.167
My boys, yeah.
-And you're --

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:45.367
By the way,
you're great in "Sing 2."

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:46.868
The cast is incredible.
-Thank you.

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:49.534
My sons are very into the --
You know, they're just starting

00:04:49.534 --> 00:04:53.033
to understand what I do for a
living, so we -- we went.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:56.901
We saw it, and they flipped out
for it, of course.

00:04:56.901 --> 00:05:00.167
It's a really good movie.
And Rocco's obsessed

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:02.968
with letting people know
that I'm Jimmy Crystal.

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:05.234
He, like, stops people in the --
you know.

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:07.634
You know, there was a tie-in
with Raisin Bran.

00:05:07.634 --> 00:05:09.934
You know, I love Raisin Bran,
so I had a box of it,

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:11.734
and they've got my picture
on the back.

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.701
Well, the character's picture
on the back.

00:05:13.701 --> 00:05:15.634
And he took it to school,
and he was like,

00:05:15.634 --> 00:05:17.200
"This is my dad,
Bobby Cannavale.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.834
This is Bobby Cannavale."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.834 --> 00:05:20.467
-This is you.
This is you, Jimmy Crystal.

00:05:20.467 --> 00:05:22.501
-Yeah, yeah.
-As you --

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:25.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
He was so cute.

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:28.634
I was talking to him backstage,
your FaceTime with your son.

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:31.067
I go, "Hello."
And he goes,

00:05:31.067 --> 00:05:33.133
"He's Jimmy Crystal."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:34.467
"He's Jimmy Crystal."
-Yeah.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:35.601
-I go, "Yeah, no.
He's Jimmy Crystal."

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:36.801
He's like --
Yeah, how old is he?

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:38.367
-Yeah, he's very into it.
Yeah, he's 5 now.

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:39.601
Yeah.
-So cute. Oh, my God.

00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:41.234
-Yeah, he's cute.
The guys are cute.

00:05:41.234 --> 00:05:42.734
Not that smart,
but they're cute.

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:45.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:46.501
-Boys.
Boys are boys.

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:49.133
-They're just not that smart.
-I got girls. I got girls.

00:05:49.133 --> 00:05:50.667
-How about the ridiculous things
that you say?

00:05:50.667 --> 00:05:52.100
Like, this --
Literally, yesterday,

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:54.634
I don't know how many times --
I must've said three times,

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:57.467
"Get your shoes off my couch."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.467 --> 00:05:59.634
And, like, my 4-year-old was
like, "It's not your couch."

00:05:59.634 --> 00:06:01.734
And I'm arguing with him.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:03.100
He's like, "It's mom's couch."

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:04.267
I said,
"That's -- That's my couch."

00:06:04.267 --> 00:06:06.367
-Mom's couch."
-I'm getting a really, really --

00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:08.634
Like, very red in the face.
And I go in the bathroom,

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.267
make believe I'm peeing,
and I'm crying.

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:12.133
-Yeah, of course.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:16.300
-Can we -- How do we set up --
How do we set up "Sing 2"?

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:19.634
-Basically, I run a casino
that the gang --

00:06:19.634 --> 00:06:21.167
You know, Buster Moon
and the gang...

00:06:21.167 --> 00:06:23.167
-Yep.
-...have come to try

00:06:23.167 --> 00:06:26.367
to get their act in my casino.

00:06:26.367 --> 00:06:28.133
I'm like a Steve Wynn
type character.

00:06:28.133 --> 00:06:30.734
Like, I own this huge casino,
and it's --

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:31.801
I'm auditioning them.
-Yeah.

00:06:31.801 --> 00:06:33.100
-Maybe this is --
Is that the scene?

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.868
-Yeah.
And it's Matthew McConaughey.

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:36.634
-And Reese Witherspoon.
-Scarlett Johansson.

00:06:36.634 --> 00:06:38.367
-Scarlett Johansson.
Bono.

00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:40.167
-Bono is in the cast.
This --

00:06:40.167 --> 00:06:41.100
-Yeah.
[ Light applause ]

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.033
-That's the --
-The new U2 song.

00:06:43.033 --> 00:06:45.367
It's very exciting.
-All right, here we go.

00:06:45.367 --> 00:06:46.801
I want to show a clip.
Here's Bobby Cannavale

00:06:46.801 --> 00:06:48.968
in "Sing 2."
Take a look.

00:06:48.968 --> 00:06:50.234
-So what's the show called?

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:51.434
-What's it called?

00:06:51.434 --> 00:06:53.868
Um, Gunter, you, uh --

00:06:53.868 --> 00:06:56.067
You want to tell Mr. Crystal
what it's called?

00:06:56.067 --> 00:07:00.133
-Uh-huh.
It's called "Out of this World."

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:03.334
-"Out of this World."

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:06.234
-That's right.
Just imagine it.

00:07:06.234 --> 00:07:08.868
Ash?
-Uh, yeah, I got it.

00:07:08.868 --> 00:07:10.067
[ Guitar strums ]

00:07:10.067 --> 00:07:11.701
-A spectacular musical

00:07:11.701 --> 00:07:15.367
that takes your audience
out of this world.

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:18.968
-♪ I want to run ♪

00:07:18.968 --> 00:07:22.734
-♪ I want to hide ♪

00:07:22.734 --> 00:07:29.000
-♪ I want to tear down the walls
that hold me inside ♪

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.567
-I love this song.

00:07:30.567 --> 00:07:34.100
♪ I want to reach out ♪

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:38.534
♪ And touch the flame ♪

00:07:38.534 --> 00:07:44.000
♪ Where the streets
have no name ♪

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.434
-Yeah!
Come on.

00:07:45.434 --> 00:07:47.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
Congratulations.

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:48.200
-Thanks. Thanks.
It's a great film.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:49.367
-Bobby Cannavale!

00:07:49.367 --> 00:07:52.968
"Sing 2" is in theaters
December 22nd.

